# Throwaway Compose project rs25-mini (mini/compose.yaml): Rakazo v0.4.0 supervisor (ghcr.io/elie222/rakazo/app:v0.4.0,
# computer image ghcr.io/elie222/rakazo/computer:v0.4.0), the egress sidecar from Rakazo's docs ("Docker in a Linux VM")
# running the unmodified v0.4.0 restrict-computer-egress.sh, and an alpine "relay-standin" on an ordinary Compose network.
# Same Mac and Docker Desktop 4.97.0 as 01. Listener on the Mac's 127.0.0.1:18925. Supervisor token generated per run, not shown.
# Computers created and probed with compose-boot's computer-probe.sh (TCP connect, 3 s timeout, via the supervisor's exec API).

## 1. SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS unset -> compose default auto
up -d --wait: computer-egress healthy, data-init exited 0, supervisor healthy, relay-standin up
supervisor log: {"level":"info","message":"supervisor listening","http.host":"0.0.0.0","http.port":7091}
supervisor log: {"level":"info","message":"restricted computer egress verified"}

computer-probe.sh create rs25bot rs25space
