## 2. Docker Desktop restart (docker desktop restart)
restart policies: computer-egress unless-stopped, computer RestartPolicy=no
after restart: computer-egress Up (healthy); supervisor, relay-standin, rakazo-bot-rs25bot exited
VM DOCKER-USER rakazo-c rules after restart (sidecar re-applied): 12; INPUT:
-A INPUT -i rakazo-c+ -m conntrack --ctstate RELATED,ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
-A INPUT -i rakazo-c+ -j DROP

sidecar stopped, docker desktop restart again:
rakazo-c rules after VM restart without sidecar: 0

## 3. Boot order after a restart with supervisor restart: unless-stopped (as upstream), auto
docker desktop restart; both containers start from their restart policies (Compose depends_on is not consulted)
computer-egress  06:18:40.505 apk "OK: 20.4 MiB in 24 packages" (rules applied right after)
supervisor       06:18:47.625 "restricted computer egress verified"
(the supervisor probes after its computer-image check; here it lost the race by 7 s, which is luck, not ordering)
computer-probe.sh create rs25bot -> 200 {"resumed":true,"started":true}
host.docker.internal:18925 timeout, 192.168.65.254:18925 timeout, 1.1.1.1:443 open

## 4. SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted with the rules missing (fail closed)
sidecar stopped; restrict-computer-egress.sh --remove -> "v4 left: 0"
SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted up -d --no-deps supervisor
computer-probe.sh create rs25bot2 ->
500 {"error":"SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=restricted is not enforced on this Docker host: run infra/compose/restrict-computer-egress.sh on the host, or set SANDBOX_COMPUTER_EGRESS=open (see docs/self-host-docker-computers.md) (a computer bridge reached the host)"}
sidecar started again (supervisor not restarted); 12 s later:
computer-probe.sh create rs25bot2 -> 200 {"resumed":false}
host.docker.internal:18925 timeout, 1.1.1.1:443 open

## Cleanup
computers deleted (200), rules removed (v4 left: 0, v6 left: 0), down -v, per-bot networks removed,
images removed (app, computer, busybox, alpine), listener stopped, Docker Desktop stopped again
(it was not running before the test).
